# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository. Git detects text vs binary
# automatically; binary assets below are pinned explicitly so detection can
# never guess wrong on them.
#
# Rationale: the repo was previously mixed (355 LF / 232 CRLF / 3 genuinely
# mixed, including CMakeLists.txt and .github/workflows/device-tests.yml)
# because contributors edit on Windows with core.autocrlf=false, which commits
# whatever bytes the editor wrote. That produced whole-file diffs on one-line
# changes and repeatedly obscured real review signal. With "text=auto" the
# clean filter normalizes on commit, so Windows editors can keep writing CRLF
# locally without it ever reaching the index.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts must always check out with LF endings. They run on the Linux
# self-hosted CI runner; a stray CRLF makes bash choke on the trailing \r
# ("$'\r': command not found"), which silently broke the crash-detection gate
# (.github/scripts/scan_crashes.sh) and let real firmware crashes ship.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never apply EOL conversion or textual diffing.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.bin binary
